# Lapis-Zero: only what the image build enabled may run.
#
# The image ships /etc/machine-id=uninitialized, so systemd applies presets on
# the first boot, and Debian's default policy is "enable": every installed unit
# with an [Install] section (sshd, adbd on tcp/5555, systemd-networkd and its
# 120 s wait-online, apt timers...).  On the device that pass finds / still
# read-only and does nothing; in a container, or if the boot ever mounts / rw
# first, it would switch all of that on.  This makes the outcome the same
# everywhere.
disable *
